infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Stop-the-world vs concurrent GC
  desc Same reclamation work — paid as one long pause or as steady CPU
  compares
    - label Stop-the-world (STW)
      children
        - label Pauses every app thread
          desc Nothing runs while the collector marks and sweeps
        - label Pauses grow with heap size
          desc A 32 GB heap can stall for seconds
        - label Tens to hundreds of ms
          desc Long stalls that wreck p99 tail latency
        - label Simple to implement
          desc No barriers, no concurrent bookkeeping
    - label Concurrent
      children
        - label Marks alongside app threads
          desc Most work overlaps with running code
        - label Sub-millisecond pauses
          desc Only short STW phases — root scan, remap
        - label Write barriers cost ~2-10% CPU
          desc Throughput spent to keep pauses tiny
        - label More complex, more memory
          desc Barriers and snapshots trade RAM for latency
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
